{:edb/db-before-t 2798 :edb/db-after-t 2799 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536111 50 #inst "2026-10-09T15:15:49.942Z" 13194139536111 true] [17592186164017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384155 13194139536111 true] [17592186164017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384155 13194139536111 true] [17592186164018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384154 13194139536111 true] [17592186164018 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384154 13194139536111 true] [17592186166835 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384156 13194139536111 true] [17592186166837 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384169 13194139536111 true] [17592186166837 1020 #edb/ref 17592186384175 13194139536111 true] [17592186167108 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536111 true] [17592186167108 1100 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" 13194139536111 true] [17592186167108 1100 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n$x^{′}(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t) + e^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n$x_{c}(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (2t) \\\\ 2\\cos (2t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (2t) \\\\ 2\\sin (2t)\\end{bmatrix}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R$.\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t) = x_{c}(t) +$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot$ |  | $0$ |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" 13194139536111 false] [17592186167108 1145 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-2{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -2[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2a \\\\ -2b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 4a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2a \\\\ -2b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-b+1 \\\\ 4a-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-b+1=-2a \\\\ 4a-2=-2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\nb=2a+1.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n4a-2=-2(2a+1)\\,⇒\\,a=0.\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\nb=2(0)+1=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 1319413